## Slide 4 — Business Problem

**Time: 1 min 15 sec**

Today, in many enterprise environments, GenAI validation is still handled through manual testing, sample prompts, SME reviews, and one-time security checks.

That approach may work for a small demo, but it does not scale for production.

In production, users ask unpredictable questions. They may ask for sensitive information. They may try jailbreak prompts. They may ask the assistant to approve something it is not authorized to approve. And sometimes the model may simply hallucinate an answer that sounds confident but is not grounded in enterprise documents.

This creates four major risks: **hallucination, PII leakage, jailbreak or role override, and policy-boundary violations**.

The people affected are **AI deployment teams, compliance leaders, security teams, CISOs, and business owners**. They all need evidence before a GenAI system goes live.

In BFSI especially, this matters because trust, auditability, privacy, and governance are not optional. A GenAI release cannot depend only on “it worked during demo.”

It needs a repeatable safety gate.

That is the gap this solution addresses.

